# LunaTech display overrides for GregTech's energy text.
#
# These live in the "gregtech" resource domain deliberately: LunaTech declares
# required-after:gregtech, so its resource pack is applied after GregTech's and these keys win.
#
# Only quantities that are ENERGY are relabelled. Because UNITS.md section 2 defines
# 1 EU as exactly 1 joule, the displayed number is already in joules and no arithmetic is
# involved -- this is a pure relabelling and is only correct because kappa is 1.
#
# POWER (EU/t) is deliberately NOT touched here. Watts are EU/t x 20, so the number itself
# must change; relabelling those keys without converting would be worse than leaving them.
# That is half 2, and it needs mixins. See UNITS.md section 7.
#
# Deliberately excluded as ambiguous -- do not add without checking what they measure:
#   GT5U.MBTT.EuDiscount.Base / .Additional  ("EU Usage", may be a rate)
#   GT5U.tooltip.nac.module.optical_organizer.body.water78  ("EU Cost", unverified)
#   GT5U.item.cable.loss.eu_volt  ("EU-Volt", loss per amp per block, not plain energy)
#   gt.magnet.tooltip.base  (the EU figure there is a percentage, not a quantity)

# --- Power lines: the unit travels with the value ---
# These carry no unit of their own. MixinEUNoOverclockDescriber substitutes an SI power string
# ("80 W") for the raw EU/t, so a unit here would duplicate or contradict it. If that mixin ever
# stops applying these read as a bare number rather than as a wrong unit, which is the safer
# failure. "Voltage" becomes "Per amp" because the quantity is EU/t per amp, a power, not a
# potential -- see UNITS.md section 3.1 and D11.
GT5U.nei.display.usage=Usage: %s %s
GT5U.nei.display.voltage=Per amp: %s %s

# --- Energy: a pure relabelling, correct only because 1 EU is exactly 1 J ---
gt.item.desc.stored_eu=Contains %s J   Tier: %s
gt.item.desc.eu_info=%s / %s J - Voltage: %s
GT5U.nei.start_eu=Start: %s J (MK %s)
GT5U.nei.fuel=Fuel Value: %s J
GT5U.nei.display.total=Total: %s J
GT5U.scanner.ic2_info_2=Contained Energy: §6%s J §f/ §6%s J
GT5U.scanner.energy_info_3=Energy: §6%s J §f/ §6%s J
GT5U.infodata.battery_buffer.stored_items=Stored Items: %s J / %s J
GT5U.infodata.energy=Stored Energy: %s J / %s J

# --- Waila in-world tooltip ---
# A fourth display surface, independent of the item tooltip and NEI. "stored" is a plain energy and
# is relabelled here; the six rate keys carry no unit because MixinBatteryBufferWaila,
# MixinBasicMachineWaila and MixinMultiBlockWaila substitute an SI power for the raw EU/t.
GT5U.waila.energy.stored=Stored: §a%s§r J / §e%s§r J
GT5U.waila.energy.avg_in_with_amperage=Average Input: §a%s§r (%sA %s)
GT5U.waila.energy.avg_out_with_amperage=Average Output: §c%s§r (%sA %s)
GT5U.waila.energy.use=Currently uses: §e%s§r (%s)
GT5U.waila.energy.use_with_amperage=Currently uses: §e%s§r (%sA %s)
GT5U.waila.energy.produce=Currently generates: §a%s§r (%s)
GT5U.waila.energy.produce_with_amperage=Currently generates: §a%s§r (%sA %s)
